{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789288927,"nonce":"wSaUA7Gn2jHc+IMAG0G0HHjXhwc=","message":"Namespaces (owner, 2026-09-13): import paths are addressed by a\nconfigured namespace, not by language name. World::Config gains a\nnamespace table: each namespace names a language (or several) and\noptionally a module subset; a clash across languages in one namespace is\na registration error. Default when none is configured: one namespace per\nregistered language, named after it, so \"haxe:game.Player\" still resolves.\nWren: `import \"game:Player\" for Player`. Haxe (build macro, later): the\npackage is the namespace name. The colon separator stays; Wren already\nuses \"@hatch:\" as a scope.","files":null}]}